  "finalText": "I built the quote as an 8-second kinetic typography piece on a near-black background (#0e0e0e) in Inter.\n\n- **Phrase 1 · Design is not just** (0–2.1 s): words fade up one by one, then the phrase lifts out upward.\n- **Phrase 2 · what it looks like.** (1.9–3.7 s): rises in as phrase 1 leaves, so the two overlap rather than stack. It then lifts out.\n- **Phrase 3 · Design is** (3.5–4.95 s): enters word by word and lifts out to make room for the emphasis.\n- **Phrase 4 · how it works.** (4.9 s onward): 124 px, weight 800, in accent orange #ff5a36 (vs. 84 px, weight 600, off-white for the rest). Words slide in on a 0.1 s stagger and it stays on screen to the end.\n- **Attribution · — Steve Jobs** (7.2 s): 26 px muted grey, fades in last below the emphasis.\n\nI checked the piece with an 8-frame contact sheet, which shows the sequence and the hand-offs working. I did not run a formal layout check.\n\nChoices I made that you may want to change: I split the quote into four phrases, \"Design is\" then \"how it works.\" so the emphasis gets its own moment. The phrase transitions are vertical lift-out and rise-in, not a morph. The attribution is quite dim, so it may need a brighter grey if it's hard to read on your screen.\n\nI can try a different transition (e.g., word-level exits or a blur hand-off) or make the emphasis phrase animate more dramatically."
